==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[foreswear]]

===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|forsweren|}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|forswerian||to swear falsely}}. More at {{prefix|for|swear|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
*: {{rhymes|ɛə(r)|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|forswears|forswearing|forswore|forsworn}}

# {{label|en|transitive}} To [[renounce]] or [[deny]] [[something]], especially under [[oath]].
#* Shakespeare
#*: I {{...}} do '''forswear''' her.
#* Dryden
#*: Like innocence, and as serenely bold / As truth, how loudly he '''forswears''' thy gold!
# {{label|en|intransitive}} To [[commit]] [[perjury]].

